msgid "原文摘要"
msgstr "Abstract"

#: ../../source/model-zoo/models/clusterkt.md:15
#: 190dc7ea1a22404b81fbbe7fbc4e1c3d
msgid ""
"Knowledge tracing (KT) is a crucial technique in intelligent tutoring "
"systems, which involves the analyses of learners' interactions with "
"educational contents to trace their knowledge states. This state-tracing "
"capacity helps to identify learners' individual learning needs and "
"deliver personalized guidance. In practice, learners' knowledge states "
"demonstrate continuous evolution driven by the dynamic interplay between "
"knowledge acquisition and decay throughout long-term learning process. "
"Most existing KT methods assess these learning and forgetting effects by "
"leveraging learners' proficiency of individual knowledge concepts in "
"isolation, leading to scattered and redundant state estimation results. "
"In this paper, we propose a cluster-driven knowledge tracing (ClusterKT) "
"model, which aims to jointly estimate the learning-forgetting effects "
"based on the latent dependencies of knowledge states. Specifically, we "
"introduce a k-means inspired clustering algorithm that can easily "
"categorizes high-correlation exercises and performances into same "
"clusters. Given the inherent state dependency, these well-separated "
"clusters facilitate (1) the assessment of current learning gains drawing "
"on their previous performances in related exercises, and (2) the "
"quantification of knowledge decay over time by calculating three "
"essential forgetting factors. Extensive experimental evaluations across "
"four widely used datasets demonstrate that ClusterKT achieves enhanced "
"predictive accuracy and heightened interpretability over current KT "
"approaches. The source code is publicly accessible at "
"https://github.com/Lzhenghua/ClusterKT."
msgstr ""
